+## Resolve effective build options
+
+Inspect the exact task/profile, generated argument file and applied
+`META-INF/native-image/**/native-image.properties` in the packaged dependencies. A configuration
+entry in source is not proof of the setting that reaches the builder. With the selected toolchain
+and its platform prerequisites, `--verbose --dry-run` reports configuration origins and the
+assembled builder command without compiling the image:
+
+```bash
+# Example: app.jar embeds native-image.properties with Args = -O0
+native-image --verbose --dry-run -O2 -cp app.jar com.example.Main
+native-image --verbose --dry-run -cp app.jar -O2 com.example.Main
+```
+
+For this scalar option, left-to-right evaluation leaves optimization at `0` in the first command
+and `2` in the second. Confirm the expanded arguments, including their origins, on the target
+release. Collection-valued options and class-initialization policies have their own rules; do not
+generalize this into replacing every configuration with the last string seen.
+
+Repair the owning task/profile or intended override if it contradicts the release contract.
+Preserve unrelated dependency metadata. If the effective setting already matches, retain it and
+investigate the remaining performance evidence. A dry run proves neither build success nor native
+runtime correctness; tie any subsequent measurement to the rebuilt artifact's hash and report.
+
